- **Steps 1–3, finding catches:** chowari had 32 new reports since the last run. I also checked every boat and shop blog in the list: Ishidamaru (didn't sail on 10/28 because of strong north wind), SSM Uraga, Sunnyside, Nakane Boat, Hamachidori, Kameya and Ishiguro, plus one YouTube search. Only Ishiguro had something new and usable: an Ito Seitoku-maru trip on 10/27 (kawahagi and aori squid).
- **Step 4, building records:** 19 chowari reports were in the three bays and had listed species, plus the Ishiguro one. The rest were outside the area (the Pacific side of Chiba, Kansai, Kyushu and others) or only had fugu or kihada, which aren't on the list. I left out one Ishiguro mention of fishing at Shimizu because it gave no date and no type of spot. Water temperature and weather come from chowari's same-day conditions, and the nearby values come from Open-Meteo for 7 new points.
